  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Introducing Automatic Stand-pipes and Smartmeters in Burkina Faso and Mali</narrative>
  </title>
  <description akvo:type="4" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Delivering reliable. sustainable and resilient water services in Africa&apos;s remote rural areas</narrative>
  </description>
  <description akvo:type="5" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Uduma&#x2019;s countries of intervention have 23.5 million in rural areas with no access to basic water services. These communities live in challenging environments that make the quality and continuity of water service complex. Uduma fills this gap by providing access to sustainable water services at scale with the automatic standpipes. The automatic standpipe is solar-powered service operating 24 hours a day, 7 days a week, working with a prepaid system and requires limited maintenance. Uduma charge end-users with affordable price which is able to provide financial sustainability.</narrative>
  </description>
